		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-14T21:17:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1498,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decouple console log capture from debug server\n\nSeparate the JavaScript console log interception logic into `WindowBuild.rs` and remove it from `WebkitServer.rs`. The window builder now injects a script on page load to populate `window.__MOUNTAIN_DEBUG_CONSOLE` when `DEBUG_SERVER=1` is set, ensuring logs are captured before the TCP server initializes.\n\nRefactor `WebkitServer.rs` to rely on the injected JavaScript buffer instead of the Tauri `ConsoleEvent` listener. This eliminates the dependency on the internal Tauri console event API for log retrieval, allowing the HTTP server to simply query the DOM via `eval`.\n\nUpdate the request handling to support a new GET `/eval` endpoint for arbitrary script execution, replacing the removed `/dom` endpoint. Consolidate error handling and improve type safety using `once_cell::sync::Lazy` for global window storage and `BufReader` for HTTP parsing.",
			"SHA": "fd6648d17f6c0f7846eb45b9080b999506e186dc"
		}
	],
